## Repository observations and reproducible reads

Commands: `git rev-parse HEAD`; `git status --porcelain=v1`;
`rg --files devices tools`; reads of README.md, devices/oneplus-fajita/*,
builder/bootc-to-fastboot, builder/flash-fastboot, base/test-aboot-deploy,
.github/workflows/ci.yml and tools/liveboot/{README.md,Cargo.toml,src/main.rs}.

- README.md:139–220 records a past Fajita graphical-session boot and an
  experimental installation. This is historical documentation, not a fresh
  hardware result for the audited revision.
- devices/oneplus-fajita/Containerfile:4 pins
  kernel-7.2.0-0.rc1.16.fc45.aarch64. The image carries kernel, DTB, modules,
  generated initramfs, SDM845 ABLX shim, USB developer-link services and strict
  kernel/boot-image/OCI verifiers. There is no devices/oneplus-enchilada target
  or Enchilada entry in the device CI matrix.
- Fajita's boot image uses Android v2, 4096-byte pages, kernel offset 0x8000,
  ramdisk 0x01000000, second 0x00f00000, tags 0x100 and DTB 0x05000000.
  Its verifier checks placement, payload and DTB identity. These are evidence
  for the existing Fajita recipe, not validated Enchilada geometry.
- devices/oneplus-fajita/aboot.cfg disables activation with
  POCKETFED_SLOT_SWITCH=disabled. builder/bootc-to-fastboot:864 and
  builder/flash-fastboot:93 special-case Fajita. The helper preserves the
  current slot; it does not currently verify the device's board identity.
  README documents the complete-firmware/UFS boot-LUN slot-switch hazard and
  the pre-guard installation bootstrap limitation. Enchilada needs an explicit
  conservative policy when added; ordinary installed updates remain unresolved.

## Dependency evidence (source/config, not installed RPM acceptance)

`git -C ../blob-wrangler show 3166dbe:configs/oneplus,enchilada.toml`
succeeds at the source commit pinned by the image's blob-wrangler package.
The configuration includes physical vendor/modem/bluetooth/dsp/persist sources,
sensor data, and >=7.0 paths qcom/sdm845/OnePlus/enchilada and
qca/OnePlus/enchilada. The new image should verify the packaged configuration,
and a device trial must verify the retained firmware actually matches it.

The retained shared SDM845 Linux checkout is at
1bbf860113b28099dbd1995844046df6ef42da87. Reads of
arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sdm845-oneplus-{enchilada,fajita}.dts and
redhat/configs/kernel-aarch64-fedora.config establish:

- Both boards include sdm845-oneplus-common.dtsi.
- Enchilada selects Samsung SOFEF00 and framebuffer height 2280, MAX98927
  speaker hardware, and its own battery/audio description. Fajita selects
  S6E3FC2X01 and height 2340, with a different speaker amplifier.
- Configuration lines 2290, 7185, 7196 and 8683 respectively contain
  CONFIG_DRM_PANEL_SAMSUNG_SOFEF00=m, CONFIG_RMI4_CORE=m,
  CONFIG_RMI4_I2C=m and CONFIG_SND_SOC_MAX98927=m.

This supports reusing the SDM845 foundation. It does not establish that the
current pinned RPM contains all expected Enchilada artifacts, or that either
device's subsystems have passed hardware acceptance. No kernel or
blob-wrangler changes were made; their commits are referenced as dependencies.

## Liveboot correction to the September 13 assessment

The previous Python/kboop/EROFS `just liveboot-*` plan is obsolete at the audited
commit. Current tools/liveboot is Rust pocketfed-liveboot, delegating assembly,
boot and USB root serving to fastboop. It consumes raw ext4, matching kernel/DTB
and a separately prepared smoo-aware dracut initrd; guest writes use RAM COW.
Only Sargo ABLX and DB410c U-Boot profiles are supplied. OnePlus needs an
appropriate profile, SDM845 shim and coherent initrd. Input extraction remains
separate work; reuse #74 rather than designing another harness.

Fastboop is pinned to 1e6d64b3c375d46f2029122902f4564d36f5498b.
`git -C ../fastboop show <pin>:devprofiles.d/oneplus-enchilada.yaml` and the
equivalent Fajita read show distinct DTB names but identical probes:
product=sdm845, partition-type:op2=raw, VID/PID 18d1:d00d. These predicates
cannot distinguish the boards. Explicit board/profile selection is required;
the generic profiles do not prove the supplied-initrd ABLX recipe works.

Current liveboot README: exact fastboot serial is selected, but runtime smoo
discovery at the pin matches interfaces rather than serials. Only one available
smoo target should be connected until the existing runtime selection fix is
adopted and validated (see #93). Hosting must continue through guest shutdown.
USB-root cannot validate cable loss, USB role changes or controller resets.
Reconnects, GPU stability and enforcing SELinux are not accepted by current
liveboot documentation; require distinct results or explicitly label gaps.

