## Conclusions and next measurement

Source evidence suggests a bounded device-image integration effort for a first
Enchilada peer trial. This is an inference, not a build result or delivery-date
commitment. Verify the packaged DTB/drivers first, derive the target and boot
checks, preserve the slot policy, and establish a repeatable local Fajita trial.
Only the peer's Enchilada can accept the Enchilada boot/display path. Record
subsystem results individually; a graphical boot is not daily-driver support.

No dedicated Enchilada/Fajita tracker was found among all 26 repository issues
returned by `gh issue list --state all --limit 200 --json number,title,state,url,body`.
Related work is #74 (liveboot), #93 (browser previews), #47 (first boot) and
#46 (carrier profiles). Browser/CDN delivery, safe update activation and full
peripheral enablement should not expand the first peer-image milestone.
